{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/master...55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","html_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/master...55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","permalink_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/FFmpeg:8f3cccb...FFmpeg:55bf0e6","diff_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/master...55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/compare/master...55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"8f3cccbca4a5f1f81ab7b990ce1acc4cb7b91abc","node_id":"C_kwDOABiiStoAKDhmM2NjY2JjYTRhNWYxZjgxYWI3Yjk5MGNlMWFjYzRjYjdiOTFhYmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Romain Beauxis","email":"romain.beauxis@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-21T15:24:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"James Almer","email":"jamrial@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-21T23:30:36Z"},"message":"avcodec/opus/parser: report the duration in units of the sample rate\n\nThe parser duration is documented in units of AVCodecContext.sample_rate,\nbut the Opus parser reported it at 48 kHz whatever the rate. A demuxer\ndeclaring another rate then gave packets a wrong duration.","tree":{"sha":"3b3506c0d9fdbd8cc4ff0fb34068b5beadf4573e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/git/trees/3b3506c0d9fdbd8cc4ff0fb34068b5beadf4573e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/git/commits/8f3cccbca4a5f1f81ab7b990ce1acc4cb7b91abc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/8f3cccbca4a5f1f81ab7b990ce1acc4cb7b91abc","html_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/8f3cccbca4a5f1f81ab7b990ce1acc4cb7b91abc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/8f3cccbca4a5f1f81ab7b990ce1acc4cb7b91abc/comments","author":{"login":"toots","id":871060,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTA2MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/871060?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots","html_url":"https://github.com/toots","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toots/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"jamrial","id":2442845,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NDI4NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2442845?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial","html_url":"https://github.com/jamrial","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamrial/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"24c2676ea52dfcb755b04960ca3a9de1bee24d6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/24c2676ea52dfcb755b04960ca3a9de1bee24d6b","html_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/24c2676ea52dfcb755b04960ca3a9de1bee24d6b"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","node_id":"C_kwDOABiiStoAKDU1YmYwZTZjZDVhNDZiMjZiMGViZDIzNzRhZDI2MjVhNzEzM2U0ZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nicholas Carlini","email":"nicholas@carlini.com","date":"2026-03-14T15:39:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"michaelni","email":"michael@niedermayer.cc","date":"2026-03-14T21:01:41Z"},"message":"avformat/mpegts: remove JPEG-XS early return on invalid header_size\n\nnew_pes_packet() moves a buffer with pkt->buf = pes->buffer before\nJPEG-XS validation. If header_size > pkt->size, an early return leaves\npes->buffer as a stale alias of pkt->buf with refcount 1. Later,\nmpegts_read_packet() calls av_packet_unref(), freeing the buffer\nthrough pkt->buf. The flush loop then re-enters new_pes_packet() and\ndereferences the dangling pes->buffer; a second path hits it via\nav_buffer_unref() in handle_packets() after a seek.\n\nDrop the early return. The packet is delivered with AV_PKT_FLAG_CORRUPT\nset, matching the PES-size-mismatch case above, and the function falls\nthrough to the normal cleanup path. The else guards the header trim so\npkt->data/pkt->size stay valid for the memset.\n\nFixes: use after free\nFixes regression since 16f89d342e.\n\nFound-by: Nicholas Carlini <nicholas@carlini.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ff5166a6f35858f8e497fc2badda2dac1f2c8a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/git/trees/9ff5166a6f35858f8e497fc2badda2dac1f2c8a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/git/commits/55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","html_url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commits/55bf0e6cd5a46b26b0ebd2374ad2625a7133e4ee/comments","author":{"login":"carlini","id":1269300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE